      "title": "Validate Mach-O dependencies and rpaths per architecture",
      "message": "For a universal Mach-O binary, `otool -L` emits a separate heading for each architecture. Skipping only the first line causes subsequent architecture headings to be interpreted as dependencies and rejected, even when every actual dependency is allowed. Additionally, `otool -l` collects rpaths from all slices, so the later single-element comparison rejects valid universal executables too.",
      "suggestion": "Enumerate Mach-O architectures and run both dependency and rpath validation separately for each slice using `otool -arch \u003carchitecture\u003e`, or parse the output into architecture-specific sections before validating.",
